# Single source of truth for the px4_msgs commit this diagnostics workspace
# is built against. The Dockerfile sources this file directly (no
# duplicated SHA to drift out of sync), and check_px4_msgs_version.sh
# verifies a running container's checked-out commit still matches it.
#
# MUST be updated together, in the same commit, whenever the PX4 firmware
# running on the real drone changes:
#   1. Update PX4_MSGS_COMMIT below to the px4_msgs commit matching the new
#      firmware's message definitions (check the PX4-Autopilot release notes
#      / the px4_msgs tag used by that PX4-Autopilot release).
#   2. Update PX4_FIRMWARE_VERSION to the new firmware version/tag, for
#      humans reading this file.
#   3. Rebuild and redeploy drone_diagnostics:
#        cd ulg_analysis && docker compose up -d --build drone_diagnostics
#   4. Run ./check_px4_msgs_version.sh to confirm the built container
#      actually picked up the new pin.
#
# Skipping this after a firmware update makes the diagnostics node
# deserialize telemetry with a mismatched px4_msgs — the most critical
# checks (position, EKF, failsafe) then fail silently or report garbage
# (documented CDR mismatch issue — see docs/production_readiness_plan.md
# gap #18).
PX4_MSGS_COMMIT=a1045ec4feb6d709bdecaf3895f1d5b43a5dabb8
PX4_FIRMWARE_VERSION=release/1.15
